# What this repository is for
#
# The code that makes this application work, and nothing that any particular
# installation of it has accumulated. A clone should be able to run, and should
# arrive knowing no symbol anyone charted, no strategy anyone wrote and no
# credential anyone holds.
#
# That split is why the data rules below are deny-by-default with narrow
# exceptions for code, rather than a list of the data files that exist today.
# The list of things worth keeping is short and stable; the list of things a
# running instance produces is neither.


# ── Secrets ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Every real env file, keeping only the examples. CREDENTIAL_ENCRYPTION_KEY
# lives in one of these, and with it every stored provider credential.
.env*
!.env*.example

*.pem
*.key
!**/keys/*.example
.secrets/
secrets/


# ── Data an installation accumulates ────────────────────────────────────
# Strategies, indicators, datasets, backtest history and users all live in
# Postgres, so the cluster directory is the single largest thing that must
# never be committed. It is project-local and disposable by design.
/.pgdata/

# Database dumps, wherever someone puts them. Prisma's migrations are also
# .sql and are the schema itself, so they are excepted — the schema is generic
# functionality, the contents of a table are not.
*.sql
*.dump
*.pgdump
*.backup
!prisma/migrations/**/*.sql
/backups/
/dumps/

# The file-based storage mode this app supports as an alternative to Postgres.
# The directories may not exist in a database-mode install, which is exactly
# why the rules are here in advance rather than added the day one appears.
/data/*
!/data/python/
/data/python/__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# Anything an installation exports or a user uploads.
/uploads/
/exports/
/data-service/exports/


# ── Build output and dependencies ───────────────────────────────────────
/node_modules
/.pnp
.pnp.js
/.next/
/out/
/build
/coverage
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts
/lib/generated/prisma

/venv
/python-venv
aktools-env/
__pycache__/


# ── Runtime noise ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
/logs/
*.log
*.log.*
aktools_log.log*
/tmp/
/scratch/
.cache/


# ── Editors and machines ────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
.cursor/
.claude/
.vscode/
.idea/
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
